From 286d87c0c45abb75f7d95517359809e412350880 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 17:43:50 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 02/44] =?UTF-8?q?feat(chexc):=20experimental=20checked=20e?=
 =?UTF-8?q?xceptions=20=E2=80=94=20flag,=20token,=20throws-clause=20parsin?=
 =?UTF-8?q?g=20(M0+M1)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Behind --experimental --enable-chexc (mirrors --enable-eh gating; without the
flag, 'throws' lexes as an ordinary identifier and the feature is inert):

- Options/Option/OptionAction: --enable-chexc -> GlobalOptions::enableChexc.
- Lex: EXPERIMENTAL_TOKEN THROWS, gated in the keyword map (chexcEnabled).
- AST: ThrowsClause node (THROWS_CLAUSE), FuncBody::throwsClause and
  FuncType::throwsClause; all visitors covered (Walker, Clone, PrintNode,
  ASTChecker, ASTHasher incl. member-signature hash, Collector,
  PartialInstantiation); THROWS_CLAUSE ignored by ASTTypeValidator until
  clause types are elaborated (M2).
- Parse: decl clauses 'throws E1, E2' / 'throws (E1, E2)' / 'throws ()' on
  functions, methods, ctors, prop accessors, operators, main; either order
  with generic constraints; functional types '(A) throws (E1,E2) -> R' with
  single-type sugar and right associativity; '...' parsed and rejected;
  5 new parser diagnostics.
- Sema is untouched semantically: clauses are inert until M2 elaboration.

Tests: cangjie_test LLT compiler/CheckedExceptions/parse 9/9; ctest 49/49;
LLT compiler/Parser+Sema regression 3934/3934; clang-format clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
